From 7c8618ec90d4d80e31e47fceae5c1fdcf3162e2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 10:26:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/57] vulkan/wsi: the Horizon (nwindow) backend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 6 items 1-10 (the Horizon WSI)
Why: nothing in Mesa presents through Horizon's VI compositor. This adds
 the backend for VK_ICD_WSI_PLATFORM_VI: surface, capabilities, formats,
 present modes, and a swapchain with explicit slot ownership, two
 present paths and a decision between them that is reported rather than
 assumed.
 Four things in it are answers to defects
 docs/reference-analysis.md § 7 and § 8.1 record in the reference ports,
 and each is written where the defect was:
  - the surface owns the window's scanout registration, so two
    swapchains over one window hand it over rather than colliding. The
    reference solved the same problem with a file-scope pointer;
  - release_images cancels dequeued slots back to the compositor instead
    of clearing a busy flag, which leaks them from the BufferQueue's
    point of view;
  - the queue result is checked, so a failed present is not reported as
    VK_SUCCESS;
  - there is no fall-through: every present either queues, copies, or
    returns an error.
 It drives libnx's IGraphicBufferProducer wrappers rather than NWindow's
 dequeue/queue, because NWindow keeps one `cur_slot` and Vulkan makes
 two acquired images valid usage on a three-image swapchain with
 minImageCount = 2. Registration and teardown still go through
 nwindowConfigureBuffer and nwindowReleaseBuffers.
 wsi_device gains a `horizon` sub-struct of driver callbacks, in the
 same shape as the existing win32 and metal ones, and
 WSI_IMAGE_TYPE_HORIZON — a renderable image the window system scans out
 as it stands, with no modifier, no dma-buf and no CPU mapping.
Evidence: cross build of build/mesa-nvk with -Dplatforms=vi
 (aarch64-none-elf-gcc 15.2.0 from ghcr.io/d3fau4/nx-dev, meson 1.9.1);
 wsi_horizon.c.o is in libvulkan_wsi.a and wsi_CreateViSurfaceNN is
 defined in it. The geometry constants are libnx's framebufferCreate,
 which is the known-working producer on this platform, and the
 num_ints field is the one the reference confirmed on hardware: left at
 zero, bqSetPreallocatedBuffer succeeds and the first dequeue never
 returns. NOT RUN ON A CONSOLE.
Upstream: no — it is a window system that exists on one platform.
